From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shikosu <teovidal01@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 16:05:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Horizon on Linux: fibers, nn::hid, per-title profile, the
 runner, stubbed service overrides

Fibers switch by ret into another stack, which recompiled code cannot do: a fiber is a host thread, a switch hands control over (horizon_fiber.py). nn::hid: one connected controller, no touch (horizon_hid.py). Entries with logic in files that stand in for system services answer 0 and are counted until ported (gen_trivial_overrides.py STUBBED). horizon_profile_xc2.py holds the declared per-title workarounds; horizon_run.py runs a recompiled game. Found booting Xenoblade Chronicles 2.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: S7bis Linux Horizon layer (fibers, hid, runner, stubs) and AOT/jump-table fixes found booting Xenoblade Chronicles 2; tests use synthetic code and fake guest memory, no game data
Issue: none yet (NX2Linux, branch swann/jalon-s7bis-xc2)

